# VS-13 S1.1 follow-up (2026-05-04, addresses PR #73+#74+#75+#76 reviews):
#
# `engines.node: ">=22.13.0"` in package.json is ADVISORY by default —
# npm prints a warning but still installs on Node < 22.13. PR #73 review
# flagged that the >=22.0.0 advisory didn't actually enforce.
#
# We target Node 22 for the VS-13 stack jump. Inside the Node 22
# branch:
#   - jsdom 29 (full range `^20.19.0 || ^22.13.0 || >=24.0.0`) → ≥22.13
#   - Vite 8 / Rolldown (full range `^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0`) → ≥22.12
# So the binding floor for our Node-22 target is 22.13.
#
# (Node 20.19+ and Node 24+ are still supported by these deps; we
# just chose 22 as our target per VS-13 S1.0 PR #73.) `engines.node`
# therefore pins at `>=22.13.0` to match jsdom's Node-22 branch floor.
#
# `engine-strict=true` makes `npm install` fail outright when the
# running Node doesn't match `engines`. Combined with CI's
# `actions/setup-node@v4` pinning Node 22.x LTS, this turns the floor
# from advisory into hard enforcement at both install-time and CI-time.
#
# Local devs hitting this on Node < 22.13 should `nvm use 22` (latest
# 22.x LTS is on 22.20+ as of 2026-05). Error points to engines field.
engine-strict=true
